00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:05.840
So that first VM we start is
actually a VM with Cromwell.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.880
Once that's up and
running, it then we'll

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:12.063
start the full
pipeline here of GATK.

00:09:12.063 --> 00:09:13.730
And then it'll run
through all of those.

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:16.340
Again, the one with
Cromwell-- when it's finished,

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:19.290
it knows that then it'll shut
down as well through pipelines.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.080
So it allows you to
manage all of that

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:24.350
without having to install
something specifically.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.120
Now, if you have
a working instance

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.710
of Cromwell installed
somewhere else,

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:29.138
you can definitely use that.

00:09:29.138 --> 00:09:30.680
But this is an
opportunity we provide

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:32.690
to show how you can do it
without needing to install

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:33.565
anything on your own.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.870
So to start this
here, we're going

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.570
to clone a couple
of repositories

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:43.060
